1
00:00:01,159 --> 00:00:04,850
Far beyond the overworld lies the Endless Sea.

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:09,279
Warm islands, bright reefs, a drowned city,

3
00:00:09,279 --> 00:00:10,259
and a trench so deep

4
00:00:10,259 --> 00:00:13,109
that the sunlight never reaches its floor.

5
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:19,169
This is Beach Craft three point one, Tides of the Deep,

6
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:22,280
for Minecraft twenty six point three.

7
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:24,529
In this film we take our time.

8
00:00:24,679 --> 00:00:28,249
We visit every biome, every place and every creature,

9
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:31,449
we look at the blocks and items and how they work,

10
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:34,179
and at the end we follow the whole story,

11
00:00:34,179 --> 00:00:35,950
the way a player would.

12
00:00:38,935 --> 00:00:41,035
The journey starts in the overworld.

13
00:00:41,035 --> 00:00:45,665
On sandy beaches stand short, dark stumps of driftwood.

14
00:00:47,285 --> 00:00:50,145
Four driftwood logs around one ancient

15
00:00:50,145 --> 00:00:52,955
energy make four portal frames.

16
00:00:53,585 --> 00:00:55,925
The energy comes from ancient broken rings,

17
00:00:55,925 --> 00:00:59,775
which hide in shipwreck treasure and ocean ruins.

18
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:04,119
The frame is built like a nether portal,

19
00:01:04,119 --> 00:01:06,890
and the energy staff lights it.

20
00:01:08,834 --> 00:01:10,054
Step through,

21
00:01:10,054 --> 00:01:13,704
and you arrive on a driftwood platform high above the waves,

22
00:01:13,914 --> 00:01:15,704
with a portal back home.

23
00:01:18,884 --> 00:01:23,775
The Endless Sea is an archipelago: open water, islands,

24
00:01:24,024 --> 00:01:27,375
reefs and deep trenches, spread over twelve biomes.

25
00:01:27,844 --> 00:01:31,855
The sun rises and sets here, just like in the overworld.

26
00:01:33,759 --> 00:01:38,559
The sea sounds alive, too: waves and wind, creaking wood,

27
00:01:38,559 --> 00:01:39,839
the calls of its creatures,

28
00:01:39,839 --> 00:01:42,890
and a piece of music for every place.

29
00:01:44,609 --> 00:01:48,859
The Endless Sea itself is deep blue, open water.

30
00:01:49,149 --> 00:01:51,109
Kelp and seagrass grow on the floor,

31
00:01:51,109 --> 00:01:55,199
and bubble vents send columns of air up to the surface.

32
00:01:56,934 --> 00:02:00,034
In the kelp forest, the kelp grows very tall,

33
00:02:00,034 --> 00:02:03,604
and patches of glow kelp light the green water.

34
00:02:03,894 --> 00:02:05,704
Barnacles cover the rocks.

35
00:02:07,484 --> 00:02:10,454
The coral shallows are warm and clear.

36
00:02:11,024 --> 00:02:14,404
Between the reefs sit sea anemones, giant clams,

37
00:02:14,404 --> 00:02:16,764
starfish and spiny sea urchins,

38
00:02:16,764 --> 00:02:19,634
and pebbles of sea glass lie in the sand.

39
00:02:21,309 --> 00:02:24,239
The glowing lagoon is rare and dim.

40
00:02:24,489 --> 00:02:25,849
Glowing anemones,

41
00:02:25,849 --> 00:02:29,139
tube worms and glow kelp fill it with soft light.

42
00:02:30,809 --> 00:02:32,789
The drowned shelf is a flat,

43
00:02:32,789 --> 00:02:36,409
murky floor covered in concrete rubble: the ground

44
00:02:36,409 --> 00:02:38,619
of a city that the sea swallowed.

45
00:02:40,534 --> 00:02:44,124
The abyssal trench is the deepest water of all.

46
00:02:44,274 --> 00:02:46,734
Down there it is almost black,

47
00:02:46,734 --> 00:02:50,704
and only tube worms and glowing anemones light the basalt.

48
00:02:52,359 --> 00:02:55,039
The wreck graveyard is foggy, grey water,

49
00:02:55,039 --> 00:02:57,089
full of sunken ships.

50
00:02:58,834 --> 00:03:03,034
In the frost floes, icebergs and ice floes drift on cold,

51
00:03:03,034 --> 00:03:04,604
clear water.

52
00:03:06,159 --> 00:03:11,209
The palm isles have sandy beaches with shell sand, palm trees,

53
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:13,789
beach grass and tall sea oats.

54
00:03:14,099 --> 00:03:16,179
Hibiscus, plumeria,

55
00:03:16,179 --> 00:03:18,759
aloe and beach morning glory grow between them,

56
00:03:18,759 --> 00:03:22,489
and seashells and sea glass wash up on the shore.

57
00:03:24,209 --> 00:03:29,239
Jungle isles are warm and wet, with jungle trees and bamboo,

58
00:03:29,849 --> 00:03:33,109
tropical ferns, orchids, red heliconias,

59
00:03:33,109 --> 00:03:36,259
birds of paradise and wild pineapple bushes.

60
00:03:38,109 --> 00:03:42,569
Mangrove isles are low and muddy, with tangled roots,

61
00:03:42,569 --> 00:03:45,239
lily pads and white spider lilies.

62
00:03:46,834 --> 00:03:51,194
And the volcanic isles are dark and rough: black sand,

63
00:03:51,194 --> 00:03:54,284
volcanic ash, pumice and basalt columns.

64
00:03:56,309 --> 00:03:59,319
Some of these natural blocks do something.

65
00:03:59,689 --> 00:04:02,169
A giant clam opens and closes,

66
00:04:02,169 --> 00:04:04,519
and an open clam gives you a pearl.

67
00:04:04,889 --> 00:04:06,779
A new one grows in time.

68
00:04:08,484 --> 00:04:12,454
A sea urchin hurts when you touch it, and drops spines.

69
00:04:12,864 --> 00:04:16,774
A wild pineapple bush is ripe when its fruit turns golden.

70
00:04:17,064 --> 00:04:18,924
And a bubble vent makes a bubble column,

71
00:04:18,924 --> 00:04:21,674
where divers can catch their breath.

72
00:04:24,834 --> 00:04:26,494
The sea is full of places

73
00:04:26,494 --> 00:04:29,274
to explore: seven places of the story,

74
00:04:29,274 --> 00:04:31,324
and twelve smaller ones.

75
00:04:31,714 --> 00:04:35,524
Almost all of them have chests, each with its own loot.

76
00:04:37,209 --> 00:04:40,399
The old lighthouse stands on a rocky base.

77
00:04:40,789 --> 00:04:42,309
A spiral stair leads up

78
00:04:42,309 --> 00:04:44,819
to the lantern room with its great lens,

79
00:04:45,109 --> 00:04:46,989
and next to it are the keeper's cottage

80
00:04:46,989 --> 00:04:49,499
and a small dock with buoys.

81
00:04:51,209 --> 00:04:53,789
Saltmere is an abandoned fishing village

82
00:04:53,789 --> 00:04:55,659
on stilts above the reef,

83
00:04:56,029 --> 00:04:59,759
with huts, rope bridges, a little market and a shrine.

84
00:05:01,659 --> 00:05:03,579
Helix Research Station rests

85
00:05:03,579 --> 00:05:06,579
on the sea floor: glass domes and tunnels,

86
00:05:06,579 --> 00:05:11,139
an airlock, labs with research terminals, aquariums,

87
00:05:11,139 --> 00:05:12,529
and a flooded wing.

88
00:05:14,284 --> 00:05:16,995
Port Solace is the drowned city.

89
00:05:17,384 --> 00:05:21,704
Asphalt streets with wrecked cars, a plaza with a statue,

90
00:05:21,704 --> 00:05:23,164
and skyscrapers,

91
00:05:23,164 --> 00:05:26,894
some so tall that their broken tops reach above the waves.

92
00:05:27,344 --> 00:05:30,074
In the middle stands the City Hall tower.

93
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:35,840
The Ashen Forge is a temple of the Tidewardens,

94
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:40,050
built into the slope of a volcano, with channels of lava,

95
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:44,730
a giant forge, and a vault behind a bridge over the fire.

96
00:05:46,435 --> 00:05:49,175
The Coral Temple rests on the reef floor,

97
00:05:49,175 --> 00:05:53,195
deep enough to stay under water: overgrown and flooded,

98
00:05:53,195 --> 00:05:57,665
with a courtyard, colonnades, statues and an inner sanctum.

99
00:05:59,185 --> 00:06:02,675
And deep in the trench waits the Abyssal Sanctum.

100
00:06:02,865 --> 00:06:07,515
Its walls cannot be broken, and only one key opens its seal.

101
00:06:09,610 --> 00:06:14,270
A pirate galleon lies tilted on the floor, with broken masts,

102
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:17,540
cannons, a captain's cabin and a cargo hold.

103
00:06:18,210 --> 00:06:22,120
Its chests hold gold coins, cannonballs and cutlasses,

104
00:06:22,290 --> 00:06:24,400
and sometimes a treasure chart.

105
00:06:26,110 --> 00:06:28,550
A rusty cargo ship broke in two,

106
00:06:28,550 --> 00:06:32,340
and spilled its shipping containers across the floor.

107
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:37,245
Small fishing boats sank with their nets and crates.

108
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:41,040
The pirate Saltjaw hid his cove

109
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:44,100
inside a rocky island: a sea entrance,

110
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:48,270
a dock with a ship, and a treasure room full of gold.

111
00:06:50,110 --> 00:06:54,540
The rusted rig stands on steel legs high above the open sea,

112
00:06:54,810 --> 00:06:57,970
with cranes, containers, a helipad,

113
00:06:57,970 --> 00:07:00,420
a radio mast and a wind turbine.

114
00:07:02,335 --> 00:07:05,235
Crashed planes rest on the sea floor,

115
00:07:05,235 --> 00:07:08,075
an airliner and a seaplane.

116
00:07:08,935 --> 00:07:13,755
Small Tidewarden ruins lie scattered on the reefs: columns,

117
00:07:13,755 --> 00:07:15,805
arches and broken statues.

118
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:22,690
On palm isles you find tiny castaway camps, with a shelter,

119
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,850
a campfire and an SOS in the sand.

120
00:07:27,610 --> 00:07:31,950
Abandoned rafts drift on the open sea, with a sail,

121
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:33,780
a chest and a little farm.

122
00:07:35,510 --> 00:07:37,230
In the frost floes,

123
00:07:37,230 --> 00:07:38,490
a research hut stands

124
00:07:38,490 --> 00:07:41,820
on a drifting iceberg: the iceberg outpost.

125
00:07:43,810 --> 00:07:47,430
Beach shacks are little bars, with deck chairs,

126
00:07:47,430 --> 00:07:49,280
umbrellas and tiki torches.

127
00:07:51,110 --> 00:07:53,290
And a buoy field marks a channel,

128
00:07:53,290 --> 00:07:56,660
with a supply crate chained between the buoys.

129
00:07:59,835 --> 00:08:01,475
The sea is full of life.

130
00:08:01,475 --> 00:08:03,395
Most creatures are peaceful.

131
00:08:03,395 --> 00:08:05,605
A few of them bite back.

132
00:08:07,235 --> 00:08:10,745
Bruce the shark hunts anyone who swims.

133
00:08:10,895 --> 00:08:12,495
On your raft you are safe,

134
00:08:12,495 --> 00:08:15,095
but your raft is not: he circles it

135
00:08:15,095 --> 00:08:16,455
and bites the edge foundations,

136
00:08:16,455 --> 00:08:21,725
until one breaks. Reinforced foundations are never bitten.

137
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:27,120
The hammerhead is bigger and tougher, and lives in the deep,

138
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,490
open sea.

139
00:08:30,210 --> 00:08:32,620
The whale is a gentle giant.

140
00:08:33,070 --> 00:08:35,830
It cruises a few blocks below the surface,

141
00:08:35,830 --> 00:08:39,560
comes up to breathe and spout, and sings now and then.

142
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:44,960
Manta rays glide through the warm shallows in slow,

143
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,150
wide loops.

144
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:50,210
Jellyfish drift and pulse.

145
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:53,740
Moon jellies are white, crimson jellies red,

146
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:56,940
and glow jellies light up the dark lagoons.

147
00:08:56,940 --> 00:09:00,010
Their touch stings, unless you wear a wetsuit.

148
00:09:01,610 --> 00:09:03,660
In the darkness of the trench,

149
00:09:03,990 --> 00:09:06,720
the anglerfish waits with its glowing lure,

150
00:09:06,870 --> 00:09:08,620
then darts forward to bite.

151
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:14,050
Moray eels hide in holes in the reefs and ruins,

152
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:15,660
with only their head showing,

153
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:19,370
and lunge at anyone who swims too close.

154
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:24,190
On the beaches, crabs scuttle sideways.

155
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:28,130
Sprint towards one, and it digs itself into the sand.

156
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:33,190
Ember crabs live on the volcanic isles.

157
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:36,350
Up close they attack, and set you on fire.

158
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:42,210
Seagulls fly in flocks over islands and rafts.

159
00:09:42,210 --> 00:09:44,750
They peck at crops and snatch food from the ground,

160
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:47,620
unless a scarecrow stands nearby.

161
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:51,920
Penguins waddle over the frost floes,

162
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:55,510
slide on their bellies and dive for fish.

163
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:59,100
Sea otters float on their backs

164
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:02,810
in the kelp forest and crack shells on their bellies.

165
00:10:03,340 --> 00:10:06,040
Feed one a seashell, and it follows you,

166
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:08,010
and brings you pearls.

167
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:12,390
And the drowned corsairs are the cursed crew

168
00:10:12,390 --> 00:10:14,410
of the pirate Saltjaw.

169
00:10:14,410 --> 00:10:19,480
They swim, fight with cutlasses, and even climb onto rafts.

170
00:10:22,385 --> 00:10:24,165
Now to the blocks and items,

171
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:26,795
in the order a player finds them.

172
00:10:27,325 --> 00:10:31,265
First the Seafarer's Almanac: it explains everything,

173
00:10:31,265 --> 00:10:34,795
chapter by chapter, with a page for every creature.

174
00:10:36,460 --> 00:10:39,850
The tools of raft survival are still here.

175
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:43,220
The item catcher fishes debris out of the water,

176
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:46,960
the water purifier turns sea water into fresh water,

177
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:50,270
and the simple grill cooks two foods at once.

178
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:56,860
Crop plots never dry out, pineapples grow from their crowns,

179
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:59,450
and a scarecrow keeps the seagulls away.

180
00:11:01,110 --> 00:11:05,990
And the Raft tab of Beach Craft two: driftwood and palm wood,

181
00:11:05,990 --> 00:11:08,810
raft foundations, the survival tools,

182
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:10,440
titanium and the machines.

183
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:16,440
The palm boat and the driftwood raft work like vanilla boats,

184
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:19,280
with or without a chest, and in a boat,

185
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:21,510
the paddle gives you a push.

186
00:11:23,310 --> 00:11:26,860
The expedition raft is made from six foundations,

187
00:11:27,290 --> 00:11:28,960
two rope and a paddle.

188
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:31,090
It is a big three by three raft,

189
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:34,720
with four seats and twenty seven storage slots.

190
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:39,480
It never sinks, it never tips over, and sharks cannot hurt it.

191
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:45,150
Upgrades go right onto the raft, and every one of them shows.

192
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:49,970
The sail makes it faster, the engine more than twice as fast,

193
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:54,100
the cargo crate adds storage, lanterns light it up,

194
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:56,050
and the anchor holds it in place.

195
00:11:57,885 --> 00:12:00,335
For the deep there is diving gear.

196
00:12:00,685 --> 00:12:02,925
The diving helmet lets you see far under water,

197
00:12:02,925 --> 00:12:06,755
and with an oxygen tank you breathe from the tank.

198
00:12:07,085 --> 00:12:09,795
A gauge shows how much air is left.

199
00:12:11,535 --> 00:12:14,055
The wetsuit lets you mine faster under water

200
00:12:14,055 --> 00:12:16,165
and keeps jellyfish away,

201
00:12:16,415 --> 00:12:18,585
flippers make you swim much faster,

202
00:12:18,835 --> 00:12:21,405
and the full set gives you dolphin's grace.

203
00:12:23,210 --> 00:12:26,950
Crafted with an angler lure, the helmet gets a lamp,

204
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:29,700
and the dark trench becomes visible.

205
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:33,520
The air compressor refills tanks,

206
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:36,610
with energy or with its hand crank.

207
00:12:38,335 --> 00:12:43,235
The harpoon gun shoots harpoons, eight damage under water,

208
00:12:43,235 --> 00:12:45,235
and the sea scooter pulls you through the deep,

209
00:12:45,235 --> 00:12:48,505
for almost four minutes on one charge.

210
00:12:50,235 --> 00:12:53,515
The wind turbine makes energy high above the sea,

211
00:12:53,515 --> 00:12:55,795
and the solar panel by day.

212
00:12:55,795 --> 00:12:59,085
Cables carry it to batteries and machines.

213
00:13:01,110 --> 00:13:04,010
The machines of Beach Craft two still run

214
00:13:04,010 --> 00:13:06,340
on energy: the quarry,

215
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:10,060
the chunk destroyer, and the brick and titanium furnaces.

216
00:13:11,810 --> 00:13:15,730
The ship cannon fires cannonballs about forty blocks far,

217
00:13:15,730 --> 00:13:18,000
without breaking any blocks.

218
00:13:19,810 --> 00:13:23,270
Building: weathered and teak wood, sea glass,

219
00:13:23,270 --> 00:13:27,020
coral stone and tidestone, cracked concrete and asphalt,

220
00:13:27,650 --> 00:13:29,850
steel hulls, beams, catwalks,

221
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:31,880
shipping containers and portholes.

222
00:13:33,435 --> 00:13:38,035
Decoration: paper lanterns in nine colours, string lights,

223
00:13:38,035 --> 00:13:40,715
buoys and neon tubes, furniture,

224
00:13:40,715 --> 00:13:43,505
treasure chests and everything a pirate needs.

225
00:13:45,135 --> 00:13:49,535
Nature: the sands, plants, flowers and sea life of the biomes,

226
00:13:49,535 --> 00:13:51,825
and the things they give you.

227
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:56,740
Chairs, cushions and deck chairs can be sat on,

228
00:13:56,740 --> 00:14:00,710
and the hammock is a real bed: it sets your spawn point.

229
00:14:02,385 --> 00:14:05,395
And when night falls, the lights come alive.

230
00:14:07,935 --> 00:14:08,875
All in all,

231
00:14:08,875 --> 00:14:12,585
Beach Craft adds more than three hundred blocks and items,

232
00:14:13,015 --> 00:14:15,265
sorted into six new creative tabs,

233
00:14:15,595 --> 00:14:18,925
plus the tab of Beach Craft two.

234
00:14:19,585 --> 00:14:23,645
Voyage: the boats, the expedition raft with its upgrades,

235
00:14:23,645 --> 00:14:25,395
and the diving gear.

236
00:14:26,910 --> 00:14:30,840
Creatures: the spawn eggs, and what the creatures drop.

237
00:14:32,310 --> 00:14:36,710
Tides of the Deep: the story items, the four sigils,

238
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:40,040
the blocks of the sanctum, and the treasures of the Leviathan.

239
00:14:41,785 --> 00:14:45,835
Research terminals still show the logs of the expedition,

240
00:14:46,225 --> 00:14:50,115
and old radios crackle with broadcasts from long ago.

241
00:14:53,410 --> 00:14:55,690
Since version three point one,

242
00:14:55,690 --> 00:14:57,870
you can also build your own raft,

243
00:14:57,870 --> 00:15:02,300
block by block: foundations on the water, a helm, and sails,

244
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:04,780
oars or a motor to move it.

245
00:15:06,385 --> 00:15:09,255
Use the helm, and the raft sets sail.

246
00:15:09,425 --> 00:15:11,535
Everything on it sails along.

247
00:15:13,310 --> 00:15:15,610
And everything on board keeps working

248
00:15:15,610 --> 00:15:17,930
at sea: chests and furnaces,

249
00:15:17,930 --> 00:15:20,540
growing crops, levers and lamps.

250
00:15:20,910 --> 00:15:22,460
You can even keep building.

251
00:15:24,210 --> 00:15:27,180
At the helm you steer with the movement keys.

252
00:15:27,830 --> 00:15:29,010
Use the wheel once more,

253
00:15:29,010 --> 00:15:32,820
and the raft drops anchor and turns back into blocks.

254
00:15:36,135 --> 00:15:39,645
A few people stayed behind on the Endless Sea.

255
00:15:40,055 --> 00:15:42,555
Talk to them, and they tell you who they are,

256
00:15:42,555 --> 00:15:45,825
what you should do next, and the rumours they have heard.

257
00:15:46,215 --> 00:15:49,365
Most of them trade, for pirate gold and pearls.

258
00:15:51,010 --> 00:15:53,390
Keeper Tobias Fenn still lives

259
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:55,720
in the cottage beside the old lighthouse.

260
00:15:56,250 --> 00:16:00,460
He welcomes you with a spyglass, points you on to Saltmere,

261
00:16:00,670 --> 00:16:05,000
buys your fish, and sells candles, lanterns and glowstone.

262
00:16:06,910 --> 00:16:08,490
In Saltmere,

263
00:16:08,490 --> 00:16:11,860
Nalu keeps the shrine lamps of his grandmother burning.

264
00:16:12,290 --> 00:16:14,850
He gives you a potion of water breathing for the reef,

265
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:19,450
and trades the crafts of the village for pearls: lanterns,

266
00:16:19,450 --> 00:16:23,240
rugs, wind chimes, and a spare diving helmet.

267
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:29,500
Old Tamo has fished from the pier of Saltmere for sixty years.

268
00:16:29,830 --> 00:16:33,240
He hands you a supper of cooked cod, buys fish,

269
00:16:33,690 --> 00:16:36,040
crab claws and eel for pirate gold,

270
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:39,450
and sells a lucky fishing rod, glow kelp,

271
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:41,760
sea pickles and even a palm boat.

272
00:16:43,610 --> 00:16:47,200
Doctor Imara Voss cracked the Tide Seal,

273
00:16:47,450 --> 00:16:49,010
and now she studies the tablets

274
00:16:49,010 --> 00:16:51,580
in the storeroom of the Ashen Forge.

275
00:16:52,210 --> 00:16:53,580
She does not trade,

276
00:16:53,770 --> 00:16:54,950
but she gives you a potion

277
00:16:54,950 --> 00:16:57,920
of fire resistance for the river of lava,

278
00:16:58,150 --> 00:17:00,180
and another one if you lose it.

279
00:17:01,985 --> 00:17:05,015
Kai is the castaway who wrote the SOS.

280
00:17:05,785 --> 00:17:09,015
He waits by his campfire and hopes you brought biscuits,

281
00:17:09,305 --> 00:17:13,765
and he trades everything that washes up, bottle letters, rope,

282
00:17:13,765 --> 00:17:17,135
plastic, scrap and supply barrels, for cookies.

283
00:17:19,285 --> 00:17:22,595
Teo runs the last bar on the Endless Sea.

284
00:17:22,925 --> 00:17:26,195
The first drink, a piña colada, is on the house.

285
00:17:26,445 --> 00:17:30,085
He sells drinks and island food, and buys pineapples,

286
00:17:30,085 --> 00:17:31,535
coconuts and rum.

287
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:37,040
Patience Okafor is the chief engineer of the old rig,

288
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:39,070
and the only crew left.

289
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:43,780
She gives you a spare circuit board, sells scrap, redstone,

290
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:46,520
cables, circuit boards, titanium and batteries,

291
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:49,790
and buys copper, iron and plastic.

292
00:17:51,885 --> 00:17:54,445
And Doctor Elin Lund studies the weather

293
00:17:54,445 --> 00:17:57,095
and the wildlife at the iceberg outpost.

294
00:17:57,685 --> 00:18:01,635
She offers you a cup of tea with honey, sells harpoons,

295
00:18:01,825 --> 00:18:06,265
wetsuits, flippers and oxygen tanks, and buys jellies,

296
00:18:06,265 --> 00:18:09,515
angler lures, shark teeth and leviathan scales.

297
00:18:13,135 --> 00:18:16,315
Now let us follow the story, the way a player would.

298
00:18:16,315 --> 00:18:18,845
From here on, there are spoilers.

299
00:18:20,935 --> 00:18:25,235
On the arrival platform waits a castaway chest: a note

300
00:18:25,235 --> 00:18:27,055
from Captain Rhea Marlow,

301
00:18:27,055 --> 00:18:31,465
the expedition journal, a chart, and a basic kit to survive.

302
00:18:34,610 --> 00:18:38,380
The expedition journal always knows the next goal.

303
00:18:38,630 --> 00:18:40,680
The first one is the Old Lighthouse.

304
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:45,470
With a raft and the chart, you set sail.

305
00:18:47,635 --> 00:18:50,185
The lighthouse stands on its island.

306
00:18:50,575 --> 00:18:54,035
In the keeper's cottage lies the logbook of Tobias Fenn,

307
00:18:54,035 --> 00:18:57,505
and a chart to the stilt village of Saltmere.

308
00:19:00,385 --> 00:19:04,915
In Saltmere, the elder's hut holds Nana Kalea's letters,

309
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:07,395
a diving helmet and the next chart.

310
00:19:07,825 --> 00:19:08,725
And behind the statue

311
00:19:08,725 --> 00:19:12,735
in the shrine lies the first sigil: the Coral Sigil.

312
00:19:15,010 --> 00:19:19,750
Deep below, at Helix Station, the terminals of Dr.

313
00:19:19,750 --> 00:19:23,370
Imara Voss tell how the expedition drilled into the abyss,

314
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:28,080
and woke something. Her lab vault holds the Pearl Sigil.

315
00:19:30,385 --> 00:19:34,365
In Port Solace, Mayor Crane sealed the Storm Sigil

316
00:19:34,365 --> 00:19:37,455
in a vault near the top of the City Hall tower.

317
00:19:39,685 --> 00:19:41,555
In the Ashen Forge,

318
00:19:41,785 --> 00:19:44,935
the Ember Sigil waits beyond the river of fire.

319
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:49,460
With all four sigils,

320
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:53,190
the altar of the Coral Temple forges the Tidewarden Key.

321
00:19:55,335 --> 00:19:59,235
The key opens the Tide Seal of the Abyssal Sanctum.

322
00:19:59,235 --> 00:20:03,505
Behind it lies a dome full of air, around a deep pool.

323
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:08,320
At the altar on the edge of the pool,

324
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:09,970
the key wakes the Leviathan,

325
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:13,710
a colossal sea serpent with six hundred health.

326
00:20:16,035 --> 00:20:19,335
It circles in the pool, where nothing can hurt it.

327
00:20:19,335 --> 00:20:21,925
It rises, and spits brine bolts.

328
00:20:23,885 --> 00:20:27,185
It leaps across the stone ring, slams down,

329
00:20:27,185 --> 00:20:29,895
and lies stranded for four seconds.

330
00:20:30,345 --> 00:20:32,035
That is the moment to strike.

331
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:37,480
Below half health, it roars and calls the tidelings,

332
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:41,550
and stirs a whirlpool that pulls you towards the pool.

333
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:44,810
Below a quarter, it gets faster still.

334
00:20:46,910 --> 00:20:49,980
When it falls, it leaves the Heart of the Tide,

335
00:20:50,230 --> 00:20:52,580
leviathan scales, and its trophy.

336
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:56,700
Placed in the water,

337
00:20:56,700 --> 00:20:58,160
the Heart of the Tide gives every

338
00:20:58,160 --> 00:21:01,870
swimmer nearby conduit power and dolphin's grace.

339
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:07,375
Four scales, titanium and a trident make the Tidebreaker.

340
00:21:08,235 --> 00:21:10,985
And the journal has one last entry.

341
00:21:11,155 --> 00:21:12,325
The sea is calm.

342
00:21:12,635 --> 00:21:14,585
Thank you, keeper of the tides.

343
00:21:17,060 --> 00:21:20,010
This was Beach Craft three point one.

344
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:23,510
Free on CurseForge, the link is in the description.

